    "standardized_narrative": "During 2022, Syndicate 623 experienced a net release of $9.3 million in prior year reserves, representing a 0.85% release relative to opening gross claims outstanding. This net release was driven by favorable claims development in the MAP Risks and Property Risks divisions, partially offset by adverse development in the Cyber Risks division on the 2020 underwriting year. Prior years of account, particularly 2020 and 2021, were impacted by events such as COVID-19 pandemic losses, natural catastrophes including Hurricanes Ida, Laura, Uri, Ian, and various flooding catastrophes, as well as geopolitical events like the war in Ukraine and the Volker hail event.",
